aquinas-st-i-ii-4.md:1: argue/answered: S6: answered no, which keeps aquinas-st-i-ii-4.logic.r2 and aquinas-st-i-ii-4.logic.r2.2, to: Suppose "man may merit from man, before he has received anything from him, by what he has received from God" is false. Is S6, "But man may merit from man, before he has received anything from him, by what he has received from God.", true then?
