aquinas-st-i-ii-4.logic.r2: argue/readings: U1: aquinas-st-i-ii-4.logic.r2 takes for granted "if a man receives all his power of well-doing from God, and not from man, then a man can merit nothing from God except by His gift"; aquinas-st-i-ii-4.logic.r2.2 and aquinas-st-i-ii-4.logic.r2.3 do not
aquinas-st-i-ii-4.logic.r2: argue/answered: U1: answered yes, which keeps aquinas-st-i-ii-4.logic.r2, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "if a man receives all his power of well-doing from God, and not from man, then a man can merit nothing from God except by His gift"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument.
